WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.680 --> 00:00:05.759
I've been sounding the alarm now for more
than a year that YouTube is becoming corporate

00:00:05.759 --> 00:00:06.759
media.

00:00:06.759 --> 00:00:11.420
That channels like the David Pakman show and
others are starting to be strangled.

00:00:11.420 --> 00:00:14.960
And I even identified the specific metrics
that confirmed this.

00:00:14.960 --> 00:00:19.830
And now YouTube is not, not only admitting
it, they are bragging about it like it's a

00:00:19.830 --> 00:00:23.050
really good thing and I'm going to talk about
that.

00:00:23.050 --> 00:00:30.460
So let's reset the David Pakman show depends
on YouTube recommending our videos to viewers.

00:00:30.460 --> 00:00:31.460
Okay.

00:00:31.460 --> 00:00:36.020
We have a nice YouTube channel, nearly 800,000
subscribers, thanks to you.

00:00:36.020 --> 00:00:40.850
But historically, the way that our channel
has grown is that somebody will watch a CNN

00:00:40.850 --> 00:00:44.800
video or they'll watch another independent
video they might want, might watch Sam Cedar

00:00:44.800 --> 00:00:52.120
for example, and then some of those people
would get the idea of watching a David Pakman

00:00:52.120 --> 00:00:57.790
show video after that by the recommendations
that show up on the side or below that YouTube

00:00:57.790 --> 00:00:58.850
suggests.

00:00:58.850 --> 00:01:03.470
And then some people would click onto the
David Pakman show video and then some portion

00:01:03.470 --> 00:01:07.060
of those would say, I like this, I'm going
to hit subscribe.

00:01:07.060 --> 00:01:09.350
Now we've got a new subscriber.

00:01:09.350 --> 00:01:16.070
Now, historically, anywhere from 50 to 70%
of our monthly viewers are not from our existing

00:01:16.070 --> 00:01:17.080
subscriber base.

00:01:17.080 --> 00:01:21.240
So we really depend on YouTube doing that.

00:01:21.240 --> 00:01:22.240
So what happened?

00:01:22.240 --> 00:01:26.490
Well, what you have to understand is that
when you were dealing with a corporation that

00:01:26.490 --> 00:01:31.820
is doing stuff and it knows that a lot of
people will be furious about the things that

00:01:31.820 --> 00:01:32.820
they are doing.

00:01:32.820 --> 00:01:34.610
They don't just tell you what they're doing.

00:01:34.610 --> 00:01:39.430
They use sort of like coded corporate English,
I would call it if someone was speaking Spanish

00:01:39.430 --> 00:01:43.720
and you spoke English, you'd need a translator
to from Spanish to English.

00:01:43.720 --> 00:01:49.380
In the same way, if you are listening to corporate
coated English and you just want to understand

00:01:49.380 --> 00:01:52.040
like normal person English, it needs a translation.

00:01:52.040 --> 00:01:58.090
So late last year in 2018 YouTube said we
will start prioritizing authoritative sources.

00:01:58.090 --> 00:02:00.980
Oh well that sounds kind of reasonable, right?

00:02:00.980 --> 00:02:05.409
They said, yeah, we're going to prioritize
authoritative sources so that we're not promoting

00:02:05.409 --> 00:02:09.289
hate speech or content that violates terms
and conditions.

00:02:09.289 --> 00:02:14.499
What they mean by authoritative is corporate
media over independent media like the David

00:02:14.499 --> 00:02:17.650
Pakman show, and we got crushed.

00:02:17.650 --> 00:02:22.749
We actually saw the views that were coming
from YouTube recommendations algorithm, a

00:02:22.749 --> 00:02:29.180
drop from roughly 4 million views per month
to somewhere between one and one and a half

00:02:29.180 --> 00:02:34.519
million views per month for a channel like
ours to instantly lose two and a half million

00:02:34.519 --> 00:02:35.849
views per month.

00:02:35.849 --> 00:02:37.840
It's a lot of money, so a lot of money.

00:02:37.840 --> 00:02:39.659
So I've been quiet about this for months.

00:02:39.659 --> 00:02:43.599
We've been grinding it out, doing our videos,
doing our show, because I can't do a damn

00:02:43.599 --> 00:02:44.599
thing about it.

00:02:44.599 --> 00:02:49.559
I told you some months ago that I don't want
to annoy the audience with this stuff because

00:02:49.559 --> 00:02:54.169
every time I do a story about this, I know
I'm spending some of my political capital

00:02:54.169 --> 00:02:58.989
with my audience because there are people
who get annoyed by these stories and some

00:02:58.989 --> 00:03:03.810
of you evaporate every time I talk about this,
but it's getting worse and YouTube is now

00:03:03.810 --> 00:03:09.409
confirming that they are doing this and the
effect is brutal.

00:03:09.409 --> 00:03:12.700
So again, we have to interpret corporate speak.

00:03:12.700 --> 00:03:18.599
Now the terms we have to interpret our borderline
content and what it means that YouTube claims

00:03:18.599 --> 00:03:26.089
that they are succeeding, that their policy
is working to stifle borderline content because

00:03:26.089 --> 00:03:30.799
when they talk about borderline content, it's
not just white nationalists stuff.

00:03:30.799 --> 00:03:32.569
It's not just hate speech.

00:03:32.569 --> 00:03:37.269
It's all the independent news content like
our channel that gets wrapped up with the

00:03:37.269 --> 00:03:41.859
hate content and not recommended and it crushes
us, crushes us.

00:03:41.859 --> 00:03:47.349
When YouTube now says that this is working,
what they mean is the algorithm changes they've

00:03:47.349 --> 00:03:52.919
made are correctly recommending corporate
content over hours and it's a disaster.

00:03:52.919 --> 00:03:55.540
Nathan recently sent me a screenshot of how
bad it is.

00:03:55.540 --> 00:04:01.340
Nathan said he'll add a ton of our videos
to his watch later Q on YouTube, but then

00:04:01.340 --> 00:04:06.189
when those finish up, the queue will start
automatically getting filled up with corporate

00:04:06.189 --> 00:04:07.189
media content.

00:04:07.189 --> 00:04:11.150
In this case, it's showing Nathan videos from
Seth Meyers, late night show.

00:04:11.150 --> 00:04:15.609
Often it's CNN, Fox news, MSNBC content from
other, you know, a hundred million dollar

00:04:15.609 --> 00:04:17.789
budget shows like John Oliver's.

00:04:17.789 --> 00:04:19.660
So I know that this is a pain.

00:04:19.660 --> 00:04:24.889
When I talk about this, I'm making a concerted
effort to talk about this much less, but now

00:04:24.889 --> 00:04:29.840
that we're getting ready to end the year,
I did want to tell you what is going on because

00:04:29.840 --> 00:04:33.910
I know many of you are watching the algorithm
and you write to me and you say, David, I'm

00:04:33.910 --> 00:04:36.240
just watching your stuff, liking your stuff.

00:04:36.240 --> 00:04:38.650
And yet YouTube keeps recommending CNN.

00:04:38.650 --> 00:04:42.629
This is a feature, not a bug as far as YouTube
is concerned.

00:04:42.629 --> 00:04:46.200
YouTube CEO, Susan [inaudible] is admitting
it.

00:04:46.200 --> 00:04:50.629
YouTube made 30 changes since January of this
year.

00:04:50.629 --> 00:04:55.099
I'm not aware of any that helped us, although
YouTube of course won't tell us what they

00:04:55.099 --> 00:04:56.099
changed.

00:04:56.099 --> 00:05:00.370
One of the issues is what is considered brand
safety for running ads.

00:05:00.370 --> 00:05:06.760
I have recently been told that anything that
mentions abortion is not brand safe.

00:05:06.760 --> 00:05:11.150
If you are an independent channel like us,
takes the issue off the table if you want

00:05:11.150 --> 00:05:12.740
to be able to monetize your content.

00:05:12.740 --> 00:05:16.699
I won't even mention the other things that
are total no goes because I don't want to

00:05:16.699 --> 00:05:22.300
get this video demonetized merely by mentioning
those things, but there are a lot more no-go

00:05:22.300 --> 00:05:25.009
topics if you want to run ads.

00:05:25.009 --> 00:05:29.009
Another issue, constant bogus copyright claims.

00:05:29.009 --> 00:05:32.340
You know, if you paid attention a few weeks
ago to our impeachment streams, we ran the

00:05:32.340 --> 00:05:35.419
house of representatives feed during impeachment
streams.

00:05:35.419 --> 00:05:38.990
CNN was claiming our videos for copyright
violation.

00:05:38.990 --> 00:05:44.280
NBC, the associated press, fraudulent claims
that crush us.

00:05:44.280 --> 00:05:47.439
I'm asking you tube, how can I fight these?

00:05:47.439 --> 00:05:51.439
And that's because appealing each one individually
is, is nuts.

00:05:51.439 --> 00:05:53.450
They're filing the men loosely.

00:05:53.450 --> 00:05:59.840
No answer from YouTube, so please consider
pushing back against this by supporting shows

00:05:59.840 --> 00:06:01.169
you like directly.

00:06:01.169 --> 00:06:02.610
I'm saying support us.

00:06:02.610 --> 00:06:03.610
Sure.

00:06:03.610 --> 00:06:05.819
Or other show, whatever show you think is
